Part of #10872
Clause-②: yes

`safeValidateSchema` (what `objectui validate` runs) and the strict authoring face accept `record:line_items`, the last ADR-0080 public block they refused at `type`. `@objectstack/spec` 17.6.0, which objectui `main` resolves, carries the block's `ComponentPropsMap` row, measured at `LineItemsPanel`'s reads, and its `STRING_ARM_REGISTERED_TYPES` ledger is empty. The arm reads that row by reference, by the batch-1 method, with the flat-props refusal and the content-channel refusals as on every other arm.

This is `Part of` the card: the `record:reference_rail` README sentence (comment `5943728376`) stays on it, because open PR objectui#11512 holds `packages/plugin-detail/README.md`.

## What changed

- `packages/types/src/zod/public-blocks.zod.ts`: `RecordLineItemsBlockSchema`, a member of `PublicBlockComponentSchema`:
  - `properties` is `ComponentPropsMap['record:line_items']` through the objectui#8317 import boundary (`stripImportedDefaults(RecordLineItemsProps)`), so `relationshipField` and `columns` are required in the bag and `childObject` is optional, as the row declares;
  - `NODE_ENVELOPE` (`responsiveStyles`) and `flatPropRefusals`: a row member written on the node is refused by name, toward `properties.KEY`;
  - `dataSource`, the spec's `ElementDataSourceSchema` by reference. The registration is gate-wrapped and `ElementDataSourceGate` puts `dataSource.object` into `childObject`, which is why the row leaves `childObject` optional. This follows the module's own rule (an arm whose renderer reads the binding declares it) and the objectui#11440 precedent. Without it the strict face would refuse the row's own bound node as `unrecognized_keys`;
  - `children` / `body`: neither-channel tombstones, from one `neitherContentChannelGuidance` string.
  - The docblock's "NOT armed here" entry is rewritten as a held-and-now-armed note.
- `packages/types/src/zod/index.zod.ts`: the barrel exports the arm.
- Pins:
  - a new `record-line-items-arm-10872.test.ts` covers the row's requiredness, the bound node, the binding by reference, and both content channels, each held to the installed spec's own verdict;
  - the batch-1 (`public-block-arms-10872`), batch-10 (`flat-props-refusal-10872`) and batch-8 (`public-block-responsive-styles-10872`, `DECLARES_DATA_SOURCE`) population rows gain the block;
  - the import-boundary `IMPORTED` list (`imported-defaults-8317`) gains the row;
  - the cli namespaced refused-at-type ratchet goes 361 → 360, with a named row.
- `any-component-union-fanout.test.ts`: the unknown-`type` bound now reads the message LESS the discriminator's `options` list. That list names every `type` literal, so it grows by one per arm by design. The whole message read 4,007 against the 4,000 bound at 204 literals. The docblock gains the new reading beside the old one.
- `zod-mirror-parity.test.ts`: one `EXCLUSIONS` row (see serial notes).
- Changesets: `.changeset/10872-record-line-items-arm.md` (`@object-ui/types` minor), and dated notes appended to `10872-public-block-zod-arms.md` and `10872-held-public-block-arms.md`. Each note corrects only the "record:line_items is still refused at type" sentences this change makes false. Both frontmatters are byte-identical.

## Measurements

- **Red first**, base `ab18797`, by a source probe: 8 `record:line_items` documents × 2 faces = 16 readings. All are `invalid_union` at `type`: the block was refused, not passed unjudged.
- **Ablation**: the union member line was removed with `ablation-replace.mjs` (WRAP mode, anchor x1 → x0). The five pin files read 26 failed, 371 passed. The restore was proved by "blob == HEAD (060da1ed48fd) and git diff HEAD is empty". The pins import `src` through the vitest alias, so there is no dist leg.
- **The new fanout bound fails on the flat union**, as the file's docblock requires of every bound. The test's parse was swapped for `z.union(AnyComponentSchema.options, …)` (the same 20 members and the same message map), and the bound reported "expected 14126 to be less than or equal to 4000". Restored: "blob == HEAD (370406be767a) and git diff HEAD is empty". The discriminated reading is 193.
- **Type reverse check** (one-off file, deleted): `PublicBlockNode` accepts the bag node. It refuses an invented bag key (TS2353) and a flat `relationshipField` (TS2322). There were exactly those two errors.
- **Content channels**, taken because the neither-channel text states this method:
  - the `@object-ui/plugin-form` dependency closure was built (11 packages);
  - a TypeScript compiler-API census of the plugin-form program (39 files, 0 type errors) found 2 `children` / `body` reads, both React `children` props of unrelated components, and 0 in `LineItemsPanel` or its registration;
  - the `@object-ui/react` program's one hit is `ElementDataSourceGate`'s own render-prop `children`;
  - a runtime probe through the real `SchemaRenderer` and registry (one-off) rendered node-level `children` / `body` markers 0 times, with the DOM equal to the no-channel mount. Control: `page:card` `properties.children` rendered its marker once;
  - the installed spec's `PageComponentSchema` refuses a node-level `children` on this block (pinned).
- `registry-inputs-spec-parity.test.ts` passes unchanged: the arm moves no booked count.

## Tests (head `efa2ef2`)

- `pnpm exec vitest run --maxWorkers=2 packages/types/ packages/cli/` gives Test Files 373 passed (373) and Tests 9719 passed (9719), VERDICT command-exit 0.
- `pnpm --filter @object-ui/types type-check` and `pnpm --filter @object-ui/cli type-check` both exit 0.
- At `b9a8a40`, the head before the two test-only changes in `efa2ef2`: the consumer sweep (21 files outside `packages/types` that read the union or the ratchet, including `registry-inputs-spec-parity` and `public-contract`) passed 680 tests, VERDICT command-exit 0.
- Gates, all exit 0:
  - `check:control-bytes`;
  - `check:new-line-citations` (0 new);
  - `check:changeset-claims` (report-only; the 21 pending changesets that name a touched file were read, and none is falsified by one arm in an existing module, one `EXCLUSIONS` row, or the bound change);
  - `check:pending-changeset-literals`;
  - `check:handler-key-reads`;
  - `check:test-path-roots`;
  - `check-changeset-presence`;
  - `check-changeset-no-major`.
- `pnpm --filter '@object-ui/types^...' build` has an empty closure (`ERR_PNPM_RECURSIVE_RUN_NO_SCRIPT`), so nothing ran. `pnpm --filter @object-ui/types build` exits 0.
- NOT MEASURED: repo-wide `pnpm lint`, which CI owns.

## Serial notes

- `packages/types/src/__tests__/zod-mirror-parity.test.ts` is also edited by open PR objectui#11512. This PR adds exactly ONE `EXCLUSIONS` row, `'public-blocks.zod.ts#RecordLineItemsBlockSchema'`, directly after the `RecordAlertBlockSchema` entry, and changes nothing else in that file. objectui#11512's hunks there sit in the `WiderThanDeclared` census summary, the `WiderThanDeclared` interface and the `WIDER_ARMS` map, so the two do not overlap textually. The seat admitted the row in comment `5972030168`.
- Two shared counters move here: the cli `NAMESPACED_REFUSED_AT_TYPE` pin, and the fanout bound's population, the discriminator literals. A sibling lane that arms a block, such as objectui#11216 in `objectql.zod.ts`, moves the same ratchet. Whichever lands second recomputes it.

## Acceptance notes

- The registration's `inputs` declare `childObject` `required: true`, while the spec row makes it optional. As a result, the JSX page compile and `validateTree` refuse a `dataSource`-bound node without `childObject` (`missing-required-prop`), and the zod faces accept it. Measured; the seat files it as its own card. `plugin-form` is not touched here.
- `record:related_list` is gate-wrapped too, and its arm declares no `dataSource`, so the strict face refuses a node-level binding there. This is dormant: the strict face has no consumer yet, and the undeclared set is pinned as a decision. Noted only.

